  "summary": "Emirate-of-Bukhara silk embroideries: giant medallion hangings in brilliant greens, pinks and oranges.",
  "description": "Under the Manghit emirs, Bukhara workshops embroidered colossal suzani-family hangings — palak, borchu and joynamaz — in silk so intense the palettes shift to acid greens, pinks and oranges unlike other Uzbek schools. Great rosette medallions, sprays of almond blossoms and fine black outlining cover guest-room walls, wedding alcoves and horse trappings of the emirate elite. Court ateliers mixed Persian floral refinement with Uzbek steppe boldness, and surviving pieces anchor Central Asian textile collections worldwide.",
